    },
    {
      "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.2/p@24954",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "PALAMON.\nHe.\nA most unbounded tyrant, whose successes\nMakes heaven unfeared and villainy assured\nBeyond its power there’s nothing; almost puts\nFaith in a fever, and deifies alone\nVoluble chance; who only attributes\nThe faculties of other instruments\nTo his own nerves and act; commands men service,\nAnd what they win in ’t, boot and glory; one\nThat fears not to do harm; good, dares not. Let\nThe blood of mine that’s sib to him be sucked\nFrom me with leeches; let them break and fall\nOff me with that corruption.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.2/p@24954/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
