    {
      "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.2/p@27630",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "PALAMON.\nLet’s to the King; who, were he\nA quarter carrier of that honour which\nHis enemy come in, the blood we venture\nShould be as for our health, which were not spent,\nRather laid out for purchase. But alas,\nOur hands advanced before our hearts, what will\nThe fall o’ th’ stroke do damage?",
